00:14:54.359 --> 00:14:57.599
But you're saying because
it's in the triple quotes,

00:14:57.599 --> 00:15:00.099
it's still reading
this JavaScript.

00:15:00.099 --> 00:15:00.599
Yeah.

00:15:00.599 --> 00:15:04.259
Well, it's-- well, because
it's in the triple codes,

00:15:04.259 --> 00:15:05.609
it treats it just as a string.

00:15:05.609 --> 00:15:07.409
But I can still use--

00:15:07.409 --> 00:15:08.999
the string can span
multiple lines.

00:15:08.999 --> 00:15:11.999
And I can use quotes
in it without making

00:15:11.999 --> 00:15:14.999
it confused that it's
the end of the string,

00:15:14.999 --> 00:15:16.409
unless I put three in a row.

00:15:16.409 --> 00:15:18.959
To Shiny, this is just text.

00:15:18.959 --> 00:15:23.609
And I happen to be sticking
it in the script tag.

00:15:23.609 --> 00:15:25.724
And so then--
actually, if I do--

